  clock: 3  # 8bc5
  nonce: 8bc5  # 8bc5
  message: "DONE in PR #2334. Each finding was first re-checked on the code (read-only probe, dev a5b3cca93); two had a different cause than filed and one was already fixed.\n1 and 2 (same cause; the filed conditions \"nothing uncommitted\" and \"in a worktree\" were not it). An explicit-path run never reached the 100% gate on changed files: the explicit branch ran pytest and exited. And \"(all files at 100%)\" was printed when the run used .coveragerc.no-embeddings: that config had no show_missing, the report had no Missing column, and the gap pattern required one. FIXED: the COVERAGE block lists every file below 100% whatever the columns, says \"no per-file coverage report in this run\" when there is none, and claims 100% only over a report it read. After a green explicit run smart-test prints NOT GATED with the merge base and each changed source file's percent in this run; --gate-changed enforces 100% and exits 1 below it (the item's ask, both halves). BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, a real explicit run with a scratch uncovered line in member_names.py: without the flag rc 0 and the notice \"member_names.py 98% missing: 135\"; with --gate-changed rc 1 and \"Changed source files are not at 100% coverage\". Before: rc 0 and, under the CI stubs, \"(all files at 100%)\". The notice costs 0.17 s.\n3 (worse than filed). smart-test tests or smart-test packages/x/tests (no trailing slash) took the self-selected path AND passed the directory to pytest, which ran the selection plus the whole directory. FIXED: any argument that is neither an option nor an option's value is a target and makes the run explicit; -k tests and --basetemp DIR stay self-selected. Tests on a fixture repository: the stub hypergumbo is not asked for a slice, the manifest is not rewritten, exactly that directory's tests run. The 5.5 min / 4.2 GB figure was not re-measured (it applies only without a stored graph).\n4. ALREADY FIXED before this PR: bfe00bcd0 (2026-11-16) strips PYTHONPATH in tests/test_generator_check.py; reverting it fails the two filed cases (re-run by the probe).\nNOT DONE (filed): the self-selected gate reads the default coverage config even when the run measured with the no-embeddings one; --raw explicit runs print no notice; the pre-PR recipe's per-package explicit runs print the notice and cannot take the flag as they are.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr3/PROBE.md.\n\nFILED FROM THIS: WI-gihok (smart-test leftovers), WI-pikuf (the smart-test playbook, a governance file, needs approval)."  # 8bc5
